bsdswitch turns a FreeBSD machine into a managed Ethernet switch, similar
in spirit to how pfSense turns FreeBSD into a firewall appliance.

Forwarding stays in the kernel (if_bridge with VLAN filtering, FreeBSD
15.0+). bsdswitch is the management and control plane: a pfSense-style
console menu, an HTTPS web UI, a Cisco-flavoured CLI (bsdswitchctl) and a
REST API, with staged changes, Junos-style commit-confirm, automatic
rollback and running/startup configurations.
